*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  dlgpatch.a -- global head patch on _ModalDialog ($A991) for ApfelPilot.
*
*  Mirrors mac/journal/mspatch.a: a code resource BlockMove'd into the system heap
*  and locked, fully position-independent (all refs Entry(PC)-relative), no A5.
*  On every _ModalDialog it OBSERVES then passes through: when ARMED it calls the
*  A5-free C walk (dlgwalk.c) to snapshot the FRONT app's dialog into the shared
*  block, then chains to the real trap. Because it runs in the foreground app's
*  context, FrontWindow / the DITL are valid there (WindowList is per-process).
*
*  ARMED gate (mirrors mspatch, per #182 review finding 4): with Armed = 0 the
*  patch is a transparent JMP to the real trap -- ZERO cost in every app's every
*  modal, which matters on real hardware (an SE/30), not just under emulation.
*  The daemon sets Armed before it wants a capture (DLGARM); OneShot clears it
*  after a single walk. Boot-installed the block ships DISARMED (Armed word = 0).
*
*  Block layout (fixed offsets, shared with dlgwalk.c and main.c DLGTREE):
*    +0   BRA.W Go
*    +4   Magic     $4450 ('DP')
*    +6   Real      (long)   saved real ModalDialog address (pass-through target)
*    +10  Armed     (word)   0 = passthru, !=0 = walk        [daemon-owned]
*    +12  OneShot   (word)   1 = disarm after a single walk
*    +14  DialogUp  (word)   1 = last walk found a modal dialog
*    +16  Generatn  (word)   bumped once per ARMED trap call (freshness)
*    +18  ItemCnt   (word)   items captured
*    +20  Truncatd  (word)   1 = dialog had more than MAXITEMS items (finding 3)
*    +22  DlgRect   (4 words) dialog global rect: top,left,bottom,right
*    +30  Records   (1152 bytes) 24 * 48-byte item records
*    ...  Go (code)
*
*  Built -model near so the BSR to DlgWalk is PC-relative (survives BlockMove).
*  Generation is incremented HERE only -- dlgwalk.c no longer bumps it (finding 1).
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        CASE    OBJ
        STRING  ASIS
        IMPORT  DlgWalk

DlgPatch        PROC    EXPORT
Entry
        BRA.W   Go
Magic     DC.W    $4450
Real      DC.L    0
Armed     DC.W    0
OneShot   DC.W    1
DialogUp  DC.W    0
Generatn  DC.W    0
ItemCnt   DC.W    0
Truncatd  DC.W    0
DlgRect   DC.W    0,0,0,0
Records   DCB.B   1152,0

Go
        LEA     Entry(PC),A0            ; A0 = block base (PC-relative; A0 is scratch)
        TST.W   Armed-Entry(A0)         ; daemon-owned gate
        BEQ.S   PassThru                ; disarmed -> transparent, real frame intact
        ADDQ.W  #1,Generatn-Entry(A0)   ; count this armed call (single increment)
        TST.W   OneShot-Entry(A0)
        BEQ.S   NoDisarm
        CLR.W   Armed-Entry(A0)         ; one-shot: disarm after this walk
NoDisarm
        MOVEM.L D0-D7/A0-A6,-(SP)       ; save everything (the C walk clobbers scratch)
        LEA     Entry(PC),A0
        MOVE.L  A0,-(SP)                ; arg: block ptr
        BSR     DlgWalk                 ; PC-relative call into the C walk
        ADDQ.L  #4,SP                   ; C caller cleans the arg
        MOVEM.L (SP)+,D0-D7/A0-A6       ; restore -> non-scratch regs as at trap entry
        LEA     Entry(PC),A0
PassThru
        MOVE.L  Real-Entry(A0),A0       ; chain to the real _ModalDialog
        JMP     (A0)

        END
